-- T-08-79 (quick task 260801-kv2) — the CHECKOUT LEASE column. GENERATED by `drizzle-kit generate`, not
-- hand-authored: a plain nullable timestamptz is exactly what Drizzle can express, so it goes through the
-- generator (the schema.ts rule — only the GiST EXCLUDE stays hand-written), which also keeps
-- drizzle/meta/_journal.json and 0023_snapshot.json consistent for `npm run db:migrate`.
--
-- ADDITIVE AND BACKFILL-FREE: nullable, no default, so every existing booking row reads "no checkout in
-- flight" by construction. Same shape as drizzle/0019_booking_checkout_session.sql, which added
-- checkout_session_id to this same table for this same one-payable-session invariant.
--
-- WHAT THE COLUMN IS FOR: a compare-and-swap claim that exactly one confirmBooking attempt per booking may
-- hold while it talks to PayMongo. Non-NULL = an attempt is in flight; the value is the instant it claimed.
-- A stale value past CHECKOUT_LEASE_TTL_SECONDS is re-claimable, so a crashed attempt self-heals.
--
-- Unqualified table name (the generator's dialect default here) so tests/helpers/db.ts replays it into
-- every isolated test schema.
ALTER TABLE "booking" ADD COLUMN "checkout_lock_at" timestamp with time zone;
